ukberi-tibyan:10-10.t:
Allah the Exalted said: {سَوَاء مِنْكُم من أسر القَوْل وَمن جهر بِهِ وَمن هُوَ مستخف بِاللَّيْلِ وسارب بِالنَّهَارِ}
His saying, Exalted is He: (سَوَاءٌ مِنْكُمْ مَنْ أَسَرَّ الْقَوْلَ): «مَنْ» is a mubtadaʾ (subject) and «سَوَاءٌ» is the khabar (predicate). As for «مِنْكُمْ», it may be a ḥāl (circumstantial) from the pronoun in «سَوَاءٌ», because it is in the place of «مُسْتَوٍ» ("equal"); and similar to it is (لَا يَسْتَوِي مِنْكُمْ مَنْ أَنْفَقَ مِنْ قَبْلِ الْفَتْحِ).
It is weak for «مِنْكُمْ» to be a ḥāl from the pronoun in «أَسَرَّ» and «جَهَرَ», for two reasons. The first: putting what belongs to the ṣila (relative clause) before the relative, or the adjective before what it qualifies. The second: putting the khabar before «مِنْكُمْ», whereas its proper place is to come after it.
